{"id":"000VWT","title":"6x6 Slithlink Sudoku","author":"RailMan","solvedCount":10,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-06T18:05:00+00:00","posted":"Heute, 12:21 Uhr","rules":"I am trying something new with this puzzle. Please let me know what you think in the comments. If you have a better way to explain the rules then also please let me know.\n\nDivide the grid into six orthogonally connected regions of six cells. Fill the grid with the digits 0 - 5 so that digits do not repeat in any row, column of region.\n\nSlitherlink Loop: Draw a single loop line through the grid along the edges of some cells. The visible clues at the start of the puzzle indicate exactly how many of that cells edges are part of the Slitherlink loop. The Slitherlink loop does not cross itself, fork off, or have loose ends.\n\nThe Slitherlink line forms part of the region boundaries.\n\nCustom fog: The grid is mostly covered in fog. Placing all of the 0, 1, 2 and 3s in the grid will clear the fog and may reveal other clues and/or region boundaries.\n\nNote: The given Slitherlink clues must be beside exactly the given number of edges on the Slitherlink line, but may be beside additional region boundaries in the final grid.\n\nSolve Online : Solution Check is enabled","solutionCode":"Row 6","tags":["Sudoku","Rundweg","Irregular (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/plt4mrpt7p","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/plt4mrpt7p","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":6,"cols":6,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-06T18:05:00+00:00"}